WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[Rapa Nui — an Eastern Polynesian language
spoken on one of Earth's most remote islands]

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:22.000
[Fewer than 3,000 speakers remain.
Most children now grow up speaking Spanish.]

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:36.000
[The language carries ancestral memory —
ties to land, ocean, and the voyagers who arrived centuries ago.]

4
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:48.000
[Revival efforts center on schools and storytelling,
anchoring identity within a rapidly changing culture.]

5
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:57.000
[A voice from the Pacific,
still spoken, still remembered.]
